1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,688
Now the part that makes this system different: the loop.

2
00:00:04,688 --> 00:00:07,033
Every morning OROS proposes.

3
00:00:07,033 --> 00:00:17,330
Every evening it grades its own call, journals the verdict, and adjusts its own risk before it is allowed to propose again.

4
00:00:17,330 --> 00:00:21,265
Inside the book today: 12 positions up, 0 down.

5
00:00:21,265 --> 00:00:23,526
Best, UNP at +3.84 percent.

6
00:00:23,526 --> 00:00:25,200
Worst, XLE at +0.92.

7
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:30,056
Both go in the journal — wins and losses get the same ink.

8
00:00:30,056 --> 00:00:36,921
The honest scoreboard reads: expectancy -8.33% per trade over 74 graded positions.

9
00:00:36,921 --> 00:00:43,786
Because that record is soft, the system has throttled itself to 25% position size.

10
00:00:43,786 --> 00:00:48,810
Nobody told it to — full size must be earned back with wins.

11
00:00:48,810 --> 00:01:04,131
What tonight's read hands to tomorrow's open: 267 names close the day in Stage 2; 1 new invalidation queue exit reviews; position size stays cut to 25% until the record earns it back.

12
00:01:04,087 --> 00:01:11,422
All figures are simulated paper trading, graded and journaled by the OROS agents with no human intervention.

13
00:01:11,422 --> 00:01:13,663
Nothing here is financial advice.

14
00:01:13,663 --> 00:01:16,652
From the closing desk — see you at the open.
